<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela to renew San Jose oil sales pact.</title>
<headline>Venezuela to renew San Jose oil sales pact.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela on Friday pledged its continued support for the San Jose Pact, under which Mexico and Venezuela export oil to Central America under preferential terms, the Foreign Ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>A Venezuelan mission will travel to Guatemala, Honduras, El Salvador, Nicaragua, Costa Rica and Panama in May to evaluate the current agreement and renew it for the period 1997-1998, the statement said.</p>
<p>Other nations covered by the pact are Barbados, Belize, Haiti, Jamaica and the Dominican Republic.</p>
<p>Mexico and Venezuela each supplied 80,000 barrels per day of oil to these countries under the San Jose accord in 1996.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Venezuela gives a 20 percent discount on oil purchases which the recipient country uses to buy other Venezuelan goods and services.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
